A||||7||Wade87GT||Pontiac arrowhead emblem||||5||
Z||000000||Wade87GT||04-09-2001||10:21 AM||||I'm fishing for some comments and a parts source. I'm just about ready to replace my cracked GT nose and I've been thinking about using the Pontiac "arrowhead" emblem instead of the Fiero Pegasus. This may sound blasphemous to some, but I never really liked the Pegasus thing. A little too 80's, like that big bird hood decal on the Trans Ams. I went to the dealer and looked at all of the 2001 models. The emblems are slightly curved so they won't lay flat. Anybody know which one would work? Any year or model, as long as it's not too big. A metal/enamel one from the old days would look pretty good on my black car.<P>Wade||||reg||5
Z||000001||kidzwheelz||04-09-2001||01:30 PM|||| The first generation Firebirds(67-69) used to have a Pontiac emblem used on the panel between the tailights. It wasn't used all three years, some just said P-O-N-T-I-A-C in block letters. If you pick up a Classic Industries catalog for the Firebirds, they sell these emblems fairly cheap. This particular emblem is flat and should work well on a Fiero nose.||||reg||1
Z||000002||c m west||04-09-2001||01:39 PM||||I think this would be the hot tip - I just might have to check that out myself<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||04-09-2001||04:08 PM||||Nope. They didn't. The 67-68 had the gas filler door in the center of the rear valence and used a phoenix (or firebird) in the center of the door which also (on some models) doubled as a finger lift for the door. The 69 had a phoenix with a key hole in the center for the trunk lid. The only arrow head was on the front bumper of the 400 models. It was a little large -- about 3 1/2 inches -- silver with black background and made of rubber.<P>I would recommend a brisk walk through your local U-Pull-It yard to look for a viable candidate. Then, just go to the dealer.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>87 Fiero GT<BR>68 Camaro T.P.I. 350<BR>69 Firebird 350 coupe (sold)<BR>69 Firebird 400 Convertible<BR>.<BR>.<BR>.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||danny boy||04-09-2001||05:30 PM|||| I used one from a Pontiac LeMans off the rear.This is the little egg shaped LeMans. The emblem is glued on so its easy to get off. My friend cut one out of a sunfire nose for his and it looks way better than anything else I've seen.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||04-09-2001||06:10 PM||||Also, the emblem's on the front nose of '67-69 Firebirds are angled to fit on the point of the bumper. <P>How about getting the rear quarter marker lights of a 67-78 bird?  They're the arrowhead emblem, but in red lexan, and the light up!  That could be cool.||||reg||1
Z||000006||87GT||04-09-2001||07:09 PM||||I think the emblem on the early 90s Grand Prixs would work.. I had a 94 and I think it was pretty much flat to where it would fit on a fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Wade87GT||04-09-2001||07:18 PM||||Thanks all for the ideas and positive responses. Guess I'll be busy for a while.<P>Formula88, about the ones that light up, now that's an idea!<P>Wade<BR>||||reg||7
